# Level 1 — click "Send Request" above each block (VS Code REST Client extension).
# Or open http://localhost:4001/api-docs and use Swagger UI.

@host = http://localhost:4001/api/v1

### Register a new user
POST {{host}}/users/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Johnson",
  "email": "alice@ift458.test",
  "password": "password12345",
  "passwordConfirmation": "password12345"
}

### Log in — look at the response headers: NO Set-Cookie, NO token
POST {{host}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@ift458.test",
  "password": "password12345"
}

### Wrong password — same message as an unknown email, on purpose
POST {{host}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@ift458.test",
  "password": "not-the-password"
}

### NoSQL injection attempt — blocked by String(email)
POST {{host}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": { "$gt": "" },
  "password": "password12345"
}

### List games (no login needed)
GET {{host}}/games

### Add a game as ANYONE — "submittedBy" is whatever you claim
POST {{host}}/games
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Hollow Knight",
  "developer": "Team Cherry",
  "genre": "Metroidvania",
  "description": "A precision platformer about climbing a mountain.",
  "platform": "console",
  "submittedBy": "Course Admin"
}

### ZERO AUTHORIZATION: edit someone else's game. Paste an id from GET /games.
PATCH {{host}}/games/PASTE_BOOK_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "I changed your game and nobody stopped me"
}

### ZERO AUTHORIZATION: delete someone else's game
DELETE {{host}}/games/PASTE_BOOK_ID_HERE
